Package: inferguidR
Type: Package
Title: Guided Inference, Power Analysis and Diagnostic Accuracy
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Raban", "Heller", , "raban.heller@charite.de", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: Plans and explains statistical analyses. Provides a registry of
    power-analysis procedures modelled on the test inventory of the 'G*Power'
    3.1 program, immutable analysis specifications that are validated against
    each procedure's modes, inputs and options, and results that always carry a
    typed status (ok, infeasible, unsupported, invalid input, numerical failure
    or reference pending) together with provenance and a reproducible R call.
    Specifications, results, analysis envelopes, advisor recommendations and
    report snapshots are serialised as canonical JSON with SHA-256 hashes and
    versioned JSON Schemas, and are imported again without evaluating code.
    Power calculations, diagnostic-accuracy and classifier-cutoff tools, a
    guided method advisor and an interactive 'shiny' application are added in
    stages; a procedure without an implemented engine returns the status
    'unsupported' instead of a number. Numerical agreement with 'G*Power' is
    not claimed until it has been shown against recorded reference cases.
